	(text
		"DESIGN NOTES\nInput 9-30 V (12 V two-wheelers): F1 fuse, D1 SMBJ24CA load-dump clamp, D2 SS34 series reverse diode.\nXL1509 40 V / 2 A non-sync buck -> V4_BUCK = 4.44 V (R1/R2). It carries the 2 A GSM bursts.\nMCP73831 charges the 300 mAh LiPo from V4_BUCK at 147 mA (tops out ~4.1 V: longer cell life).\nPower path: V4_BUCK -> D4 -> VSYS (4.1 V); Q1 P-FET connects the battery to VSYS when the buck stops.\nVSYS (3.3-4.3 V) feeds the EC200U VBAT_BB/VBAT_RF directly: 220 uF + 100 uF + 100n/33p/10p + 5 V TVS.\nLayout: buck loop C2-U1-D3 short, SW copper small; keep the buck away from the GNSS corner."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f31b2683-e311-5e1d-8504-b494b3a84ab9")
	)
	(text
		"PART NOTES (VERIFY = check against vendor datasheet before release)\nJ1: 1 +12V(BAT) 2 GND 3 IGN 4 RELAY (low side, coil to +12V)\nD1: clamp 38.9 V < XL1509 40 V abs max; reverse battery blows F1 via D1\nC1: input bulk; the harness inductance is damped by D1 + F1\nU1: EN (pin 5) low = on, tied to GND; pins 6-8 GND heat-spreader - VERIFY pinout vs XLSEMI datasheet\nL1: VERIFY Isat >= 2.2 A (GSM burst); alt. CYNTEC / Sunlord 6045 22 uH\nR1: VOUT = 1.23 V x (1 + R1/R2) = 4.44 V\nU2: Input is the 4.44 V buck rail: the cell tops out ~4.1 V (longer life in a hot under-seat box)\nR3: ICHG = 1000 V / R = 147 mA (0.5 C for 300 mAh)\nQ1: Gate = buck rail: off while the buck runs (Vgs = +0.35 V), on (Vgs = -VBAT) when it stops\nR4: discharges the buck rail so Q1 turns on fast\nC8: C8 + C9 = 200 uF ceramic GSM burst reservoir (~120 uF at 4 V bias)\nR6: VIN 0-37 V -> 0-1.18 V (ADC1)\nR8: VBAT/4 -> ADC0, 10 uA"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 219.71 154.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "074daf9e-a844-5838-9c27-84def1b3f97e")
	)
)
